Our utilization of our federal net operating loss carryforwards (“NOLs”) may be severely limited or potentially eliminated.
As of December 31, 2018, we had federal NOLs of $454.5 million that will expire primarily between 2020 and 2027, with the majority of them
expiring between 2020 and 2024. We are currently able to offset all of our tax liabilities with our federal NOLs, but we may not generate sufficient taxable
income in future years to utilize all of our NOLs prior to their expiration. If our federal NOLs expire unused, their full benefit will not be achieved. In
